iction\n  *", " **Astrolabe", "** and analog astronomical", " modeling", "\n  * **", "Positional decimal", " notation** and the", " use", " of **zero**", "\n  * Early", " algebra", "ic and algorithmic", " methods from", " Greek", ", Indian, and", " Islamic mathematics\n\n##", " Mechanical Calculators\n\n", "The first true", " mechanical calculators appeared", " in the sevent", "eenth century,", " when thinkers", " began to ask", " whether arithmetic", " itself could be automated", ". In", " 164", "2, the", " French mathematician **", "Blaise Pascal**", " invented the **P", "ascaline**, a", " device", " that could add", " and subtract by", " using", " a", " set", " of inter", "locking gears.", " Pascal", "\u2019s motivation was practical", ": his", " father worked", " in", " tax collection", ", and Pascal", " wanted", " a", " machine that could reduce", " errors", " in repetitive", " numerical", " work. The Pascal", "ine was far", " from general", "-purpose, and", " it was fragile", " and", " expensive, but it", " established", " a crucial principle:", " that a", " physical", " machine could carry out", " **", "carry", " operations", "**,", " one", " of the basic", " requirements", " of arithmetic. This", " was a", " decisive", " step from", " human", " calculation to", " mechanical", " calculation,", " because it", " meant", " that the most", " error-prone part", " of addition", " could be made", " automatic", ".\n\nThe next", " major advance", " came from", " **Gottfried", " Wilhelm Leibniz", "**, who in", " the 16", "70s designed", " the **Stepped", " Reckoner**,", " or", " **Leibn", "iz wheel", "**.", " Unlike", " Pascal\u2019s machine,", " Leibniz\u2019s", " calculator", " could perform addition", ", subtraction", ", multiplication, and", " division, and it", " used a stepping", " drum", " to", " implement", " multiplication through", " repeated addition", ".", " Leib", "niz also", " experimented", " with logarith", "mic", " scales", " and envisioned", " machines", " that could handle", " more advanced", " mathematical work", ". His", " designs", " were often", " imperfect", " in", " practice, but they", " expanded", " the ambition", " of mechanical calculation.", " For", " Leibniz,", " computing", " machines", " were not merely office", " tools; they were", " part of a larger", " project", " to make", " reason", " more", " mechanical", ",", " more universal, and", " less dependent", " on individual", " skill", ". This", " vision reson", "ates", " strongly with later", " computer science, which", " is", " often", " described as the science", " of formal", " reasoning", " and executable", " procedures", ".\n\nThe", " most consequential", " mechanical", " ideas", " of this", " era came from **", "Charles Babbage**", " in the nineteenth century", ". B", "abbage first", " designed the **Difference", " Engine**, a machine", " intended to compute", " polynomial", " tables for navigation", " and", " scientific", " use.", " He", " later envisioned", " a", " far more radical", " device", ":", " the **Analytical", " Engine**, which", " would have been capable", " of executing", " a", " sequence of operations", " based on instructions", " encoded", " on", " punched", " cards,", " much", " like a", " loom or", " a modern", " computer", ". The English", " mathematician **Ada", " Lovelace**", " played", " a pivotal", " role in artic", "ulating the", " power of such", " a machine, emphasizing", " that it", " could manipulate", " symbols according", " to rules", " and that", " it might one", " day be used", " for music", ", graphics", ", and other", " forms of symbolic", " processing", ". Although", " Babbage\u2019s machines", " were never fully built", " in his", " lifetime due", " to engineering", ",", " funding", ", and precision", "-man", "ufacturing limitations", ", they", " introduced the core", " concepts of **", "stored instructions", "**, **programm", "ability", "**, **memory**,", " and **general", "-purpose computation**. Meanwhile", ", **Herman", " Hollerith**", " developed **", "tab", "ulating machines** using", " punch", " cards for the ", "1890", " United States census", ", giving", " birth to a", " commercial", " data-processing industry that", " would later become **", "IBM**.\n\n*", " Key inventions", " and concepts", ":\n  *", " **Pascaline", "** and automatic", " carrying", "\n  * **", "Leibniz", " Stepped Reck", "oner** and mechanical", " multiplication\n  *", " **Difference", " Engine** and automatic", " table computation", "\n  * **", "Analytical Engine**", " and the idea", " of a programm", "able general", "-purpose machine\n ", " * **Punch", "-card", " tabulation", "** and the origins", " of commercial data processing", "\n\n## Electrom", "echanical Relay Computers", "\n\nBy", " the early twentieth century", ", the limitations", " of mechanical calcul", "ators had", " become obvious", ". Mechanical", " devices", " were too", " slow, too noisy", ", and", " too difficult", " to scale", " for the", " increasingly complex calculations", " demanded by science", ", industry", ", and government", ". The next", " major step was the", " use of **elect", "romechanical rel", "ays**", " and", " **electric", " switches", "** to perform logical", " and", " arithmetic operations. Rel", "ays could", " be switched", " rapidly", " by electrical", " signals, and because", " they operated", " on", " principles", " related", " to tele", "graphy and telephone switching", ", they made", " possible", " machines", " that were", " faster", " than", " purely mechanical calcul", "ators and more", " suitable", " for large-scale computation", ". This", " era was", " also shaped by the", " mathematics", " of **George", " Boole**, whose", " **Boolean algebra**", " showed", " that logical reasoning", " could be expressed", " in algebra", "ic form", ", and by the", " later", " work of **Claude", " Shannon**, who demonstrated", " in", " the", " 193", "0s that electrical", " circuits could implement", " logical", " operations. Together", ", these ideas turned", " computing", " into", " a problem", " of signal", " control", " rather", " than purely", " mechanical motion.\n\n", "Several", " early", " electrom", "echanical and", " electronic", " hybrid", " machines emerged", " in", " the", " 193", "0s and ", "1940", "s. The", " **Atanasoff", "\u2013Berry Computer**,", " built", " by **John", " Atanasoff**", " and **Cliff", "ord Berry** at", " Iowa State College", ", is", " often regarded as an", " important for", "erunner", " to", " electronic digital computing.", " It used vacuum", " tubes for", " arithmetic", " and a", " regenerative drum", "-and", "-capacitor memory", " system to", " solve systems", " of linear equations,", " a task", " important", " in scientific", " research", ". Although", " it", " was not a fully", " programm", "able general-purpose computer", ", the", " ABC showed", " that electronic", " circuits", " and", " new", " forms", " of memory could greatly", " increase", " speed", " and reduce", " manual", " intervention", ". Its", " development", " reflected", " a", " key", " problem of", " the period", ": how", " to solve scientific", " and", " engineering equations", " that were too large", " for", " human or", " mechanical", " calculators to handle", " efficiently.\n\nThe", " most famous electrom", "echanical relay computers", " of the era were", " the **Harvard", " Mark I**,", " also known as the", " **Automatic Sequence Controlled", " Calculator", " (", "ASCC", ")**, and the British", " **Colossus", "**. The Mark", " I, developed", " by **Howard A", "iken** with", " support", " from **", "IBM** and", " **", "Harvard University**,", " was built", " during", " World War II to", " compute", " artillery", " firing", " tables and other mathematical", " functions", ". It used", " rel", "ays, rotating", " drums, and punched", " tape", ", and it represented", " a major", " step toward automated", ", repeat", "able calculation", " in", " wartime", " research",